.TH CSVQ 1 "2026-02-15" "csvq 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
csvq \- deterministic CSV data-quality toolkit
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B csvq
.I command
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIfiles\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B csvq
is a pure Bash and POSIX awk toolkit for auditing and cleaning CSV files.
It has no runtime dependencies and produces byte-deterministic output
(LC_ALL=C, no timestamps or paths-of-the-day), which makes it suitable as a
data-quality gate in CI pipelines.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B audit \fIpaths...\fR [\-o \fIDIR\fR] [\-d \fIDELIM\fR] [\-\-strict]
Write analysis_report.txt, data_summary.txt and duplicates_found.txt into
DIR (default ./out). With \-\-strict, exit non-zero if any file has duplicate
or ragged rows.
.TP
.B stats \fIfile\fR [\-d \fIDELIM\fR]
Per-column type, null rate, cardinality, min/max/mean and top values.
.TP
.B validate \fIfile\fR \-\-schema \fIFILE\fR [\-d \fIDELIM\fR]
Validate against a schema DSL. Exit non-zero on any violation.
.TP
.B diff \fIold\fR \fInew\fR \-\-key \fICOL\fR[,\fICOL\fR] [\-d \fIDELIM\fR]
Keyed row diff: added, changed and removed rows.
.TP
.B dedupe \fIfile\fR [\-\-key \fICOL\fR[,\fICOL\fR]] [\-d \fIDELIM\fR]
Drop duplicate rows, whole-row or by key, keeping the first occurrence.
.TP
.B normalize \fIfile\fR [\-\-in\-place]
CRLF to LF, strip trailing whitespace, ensure a final newline.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (and, for validate/audit \-\-strict, no issues).
.TP
.B 1
Validation violations, or a failed \-\-strict gate.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error (bad arguments or missing file).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CSVQ_AWK
awk implementation to use (default: awk).
.SH AUTHOR
Midat Faizov.
